210
00:16:25,692 --> 00:16:26,902
Yeon-su.

211
00:16:27,986 --> 00:16:31,198
If I'm moving too fast,
you can trip me.

212
00:16:31,490 --> 00:16:32,491
What?

213
00:16:34,326 --> 00:16:35,952
I feel like I'm rushing you

214
00:16:36,036 --> 00:16:37,954
because my feelings are
getting ahead of me.

215
00:16:40,540 --> 00:16:44,044
Then let's go for something good
next week.

216
00:16:55,055 --> 00:16:56,723
Mr. Yun.

217
00:17:00,227 --> 00:17:02,979
I don't think
I can go on a date with you.

218
00:17:03,647 --> 00:17:07,275
I really appreciated
how you cheered me up

219
00:17:07,359 --> 00:17:10,946
with something delicious
every time I was down or upset.

220
00:17:14,032 --> 00:17:15,742
But my heart says

221
00:17:17,452 --> 00:17:19,579
that's it for me.

222
00:17:23,375 --> 00:17:26,503
Can you tell me why?

223
00:17:27,170 --> 00:17:29,005
Is it about me?

224
00:17:29,881 --> 00:17:31,841
Or...

225
00:17:32,968 --> 00:17:35,220
are you into someone else?

226
00:17:44,604 --> 00:17:46,106
My heart belongs to me

227
00:17:46,523 --> 00:17:48,316
and your heart belongs to you.

228
00:17:50,735 --> 00:17:53,530
Still, thank you
for being honest with me.

229
00:17:55,240 --> 00:17:57,117
Thank you.

230
00:17:57,325 --> 00:17:59,244
Feel free to call me
when you're down.

231
00:17:59,411 --> 00:18:01,621
I'll buy you spicy udon
as much as you want.

232
00:18:53,089 --> 00:18:55,425
Your movements are heavy,
and your expression is dark.

233
00:18:55,508 --> 00:18:56,635
What's gotten into you?

234
00:18:57,927 --> 00:18:58,970
I'm sorry.

235
00:18:59,054 --> 00:19:00,347
Are you not feeling well
or something?

236
00:19:00,430 --> 00:19:03,516
Or now that you're leaving,
are you losing motivation?

237
00:19:04,434 --> 00:19:06,102
<i>You're still a member of this team.</i>

238
00:19:06,394 --> 00:19:08,063
<i>Do your best</i>
<i>for the rest of the performance.</i>

239
00:19:27,165 --> 00:19:30,418
NAM-SU

240
00:19:41,388 --> 00:19:42,555
MY SI-EUN

241
00:19:45,934 --> 00:19:48,770
<i>- The call cannot be connected...</i>
- Hey.

242
00:19:49,854 --> 00:19:52,065
- Come and move this.
- Yes, I'm coming.

243
00:19:57,821 --> 00:20:00,031
Can you make a pyramid?

244
00:20:00,573 --> 00:20:02,826
What are you making right now?

245
00:20:02,909 --> 00:20:05,453
I'm making a pyramid.

246
00:20:08,748 --> 00:20:11,126
Mr. Yoon, how have you been?

247
00:20:11,209 --> 00:20:14,087
I heard he went to say hi,
but I haven't heard anything since.

248
00:20:14,170 --> 00:20:15,839
You know he's a busy guy.

249
00:20:15,922 --> 00:20:18,299
<i>You put me in a tough spot.</i>

250
00:20:18,925 --> 00:20:19,968
What do you mean?

251
00:20:20,051 --> 00:20:23,930
<i>If your son had a problem like that,</i>
<i>you should've told me.</i>

252
00:20:24,013 --> 00:20:25,056
What problem?

253
00:20:26,474 --> 00:20:28,601
What's that? My son is what?

254
00:20:32,731 --> 00:20:34,107
Why did you cook so much?

255
00:20:34,190 --> 00:20:36,025
You know I cook when I'm down.

256
00:20:36,109 --> 00:20:38,153
Just buy bread.
Why go through this trouble?

257
00:20:38,862 --> 00:20:40,321
I did bake some bread too.

258
00:20:45,285 --> 00:20:46,411
FATHER

259
00:20:50,331 --> 00:20:51,583
Answer it.

260
00:20:51,666 --> 00:20:53,918
Because you keep rejecting him,
he calls me instead.

261
00:20:54,002 --> 00:20:56,755
- Just block him.
- So rude.

262
00:20:56,838 --> 00:20:58,506
He only has one reason to call me.

263
00:20:58,965 --> 00:21:01,050
- A blind date.
- That's not it.

264
00:21:01,217 --> 00:21:02,969
He asked me how you were doing.

265
00:21:03,386 --> 00:21:06,347
If everything was okay with you
and if you were seeing anyone.

266
00:21:06,598 --> 00:21:08,516
I doubt it. Stop answering his calls.

267
00:21:08,600 --> 00:21:09,934
Then you answer them.

268
00:21:11,227 --> 00:21:12,353
So what did you tell him?

269
00:21:12,437 --> 00:21:13,605
Everything is fine.

270
00:21:13,980 --> 00:21:15,857
You're always seeing somebody.

271
00:21:18,443 --> 00:21:21,237
Anyway, is he still telling you
to go on blind dates?

272
00:21:22,864 --> 00:21:25,116
Wasn't Yeon-su the last one?

273
00:21:27,994 --> 00:21:30,079
I should've gone instead.

274
00:21:30,371 --> 00:21:32,665
If we'd met on a blind date
from the start

275
00:21:33,291 --> 00:21:34,876
things would've been different.

276
00:21:36,377 --> 00:21:37,921
What do you mean?

277
00:21:39,297 --> 00:21:42,050
She turned me down.

278
00:21:42,884 --> 00:21:45,595
- What?
- I think

279
00:21:46,763 --> 00:21:48,014
she's into someone else.

280
00:21:52,185 --> 00:21:53,812
I still have so much to show.

281
00:21:53,895 --> 00:21:55,522
What's the point if adults like me?

282
00:21:55,605 --> 00:21:56,940
Yeon-su didn't even give me a chance.

283
00:21:57,649 --> 00:21:59,901
Screw it. Let's have a beer.

284
00:22:00,151 --> 00:22:01,277
Sure.

285
00:22:11,955 --> 00:22:13,039
Good.

286
00:22:13,665 --> 00:22:15,708
- Are those new clothes?
- No, I've had these.

287
00:22:15,792 --> 00:22:17,210
Did you get new skincare?

288
00:22:17,293 --> 00:22:18,628
It's old.

289
00:22:19,045 --> 00:22:21,005
But something about you
feels different.

290
00:22:21,089 --> 00:22:22,173
There's nothing.

291
00:22:23,508 --> 00:22:26,135
Do I look sophisticated?

292
00:22:26,219 --> 00:22:29,389
Should I say you seem

293
00:22:29,472 --> 00:22:31,307
a bit too excited in general?

294
00:22:31,683 --> 00:22:35,019
Or should I say
I can feel the yang energy in you?

295
00:22:36,271 --> 00:22:38,439
What are you saying?

296
00:22:38,523 --> 00:22:40,525
Something happened in Busan?

297
00:22:41,109 --> 00:22:43,152
What's there to happen?

298
00:22:43,236 --> 00:22:46,781
Hold on. Why are you stuttering?

299
00:22:47,115 --> 00:22:49,576
I knew it. You...

300
00:22:51,703 --> 00:22:52,829
You did it.

301
00:22:53,329 --> 00:22:56,374
- Geez.
- What? Did you really do it?

302
00:22:56,457 --> 00:22:57,667
Really?

303
00:22:57,750 --> 00:23:00,128
Aunt Mi-young, keep your voice down.

304
00:23:00,211 --> 00:23:01,754
They'll hear you from outside.

305
00:23:01,838 --> 00:23:04,465
Finally... You finally did it!

306
00:23:07,135 --> 00:23:08,678
Dear ancestors... Where are they?

307
00:23:08,761 --> 00:23:10,430
Dear ancestors.

308
00:23:10,513 --> 00:23:12,932
At last,
the eldest daughter of the Gongs

309
00:23:13,016 --> 00:23:16,686
finally unboxed her body.

310
00:23:18,146 --> 00:23:20,064
Stop.

311
00:23:22,066 --> 00:23:23,943
How was it?

312
00:23:24,027 --> 00:23:25,737
Was it good? Did you see heaven?

313
00:23:25,820 --> 00:23:27,655
I don't know. Get away from me.

314
00:23:27,739 --> 00:23:30,491
Tell me. How was it?

315
00:23:30,575 --> 00:23:32,118
Give me a one-line review.

316
00:23:34,579 --> 00:23:38,082
I don't know why everyone wants to
hear about my first time.

317
00:23:38,333 --> 00:23:39,584
Your first time?

318
00:23:46,132 --> 00:23:47,342
Did you...

319
00:23:49,218 --> 00:23:50,261
have sex?

320
00:23:52,138 --> 00:23:55,475
I was talking about a sex toy.

321
00:23:56,726 --> 00:24:00,355
That's what I was talking about.

322
00:24:00,438 --> 00:24:03,524
Oh, my goodness. That's crazy.

323
00:24:04,817 --> 00:24:05,944
I can't believe it.

324
00:24:06,486 --> 00:24:07,612
Oh, my god.

325
00:24:08,071 --> 00:24:09,238
It feels like just yesterday

326
00:24:09,322 --> 00:24:11,115
you were running around
in squeaky shoes.

327
00:24:13,701 --> 00:24:15,370
You're all grown up now.

328
00:24:19,749 --> 00:24:20,875
How was it?

329
00:24:21,626 --> 00:24:22,835
It wasn't such a big deal, was it?

330
00:24:26,881 --> 00:24:29,342
What's the big deal about it? Geez.

331
00:24:29,425 --> 00:24:33,137
As if it were some forbidden fruit.

332
00:24:37,767 --> 00:24:41,354
Aunt Mi-young, how did you feel?

333
00:24:41,437 --> 00:24:42,647
You mean, did I feel it?

334
00:24:43,147 --> 00:24:45,316
No, not that.

335
00:24:45,566 --> 00:24:47,527
Were you okay emotionally?

336
00:24:50,989 --> 00:24:52,031
Why?

337
00:24:52,615 --> 00:24:53,866
How did you feel?

338
00:24:56,160 --> 00:24:58,579
It feels strange.

339
00:24:59,998 --> 00:25:02,875
I wonder if it's okay

340
00:25:02,959 --> 00:25:04,502
and then I suddenly feel vain.

341
00:25:05,003 --> 00:25:07,922
I feel guilty, but at the same time

342
00:25:08,006 --> 00:25:09,382
I feel relieved.

343
00:25:12,093 --> 00:25:14,762
There's a four-syllable expression
for that.

344
00:25:17,056 --> 00:25:20,351
Bittersweet.

345
00:25:25,815 --> 00:25:28,317
We don't need to
stick to our principles.

346
00:25:29,193 --> 00:25:30,570
We're just keeping our promise.

347
00:25:34,032 --> 00:25:37,118
Now, let's worry

348
00:25:37,452 --> 00:25:39,746
about our own lives.

349
00:25:42,582 --> 00:25:43,708
Come out and eat.

350
00:25:49,547 --> 00:25:51,966
Anyway, who was it?
The first one or the second one?

351
00:25:52,050 --> 00:25:53,801
Oh, stop it.

352
00:25:55,511 --> 00:25:56,846
- Third one?
- Enough.

353
00:26:10,485 --> 00:26:12,987
I hardly see my grandson these days.

354
00:26:13,821 --> 00:26:15,907
He left early in the morning again.

355
00:26:15,990 --> 00:26:18,367
The exam is right around the corner,
so he seems to be studying hard.

356
00:26:18,451 --> 00:26:19,702
Oh, dear.

357
00:26:20,787 --> 00:26:22,580
How praiseworthy.

358
00:26:22,663 --> 00:26:23,915
There isn't much time left now.

359
00:26:23,998 --> 00:26:25,041
He'll pass this time

360
00:26:25,124 --> 00:26:27,502
so hang in there a little longer,
Baek-hee.

361
00:26:27,585 --> 00:26:28,669
Yes, of course, Father.

362
00:26:28,753 --> 00:26:31,422
We'll have to see
whether he passes or not.

363
00:26:31,506 --> 00:26:33,591
That's the thing about life.

364
00:26:33,674 --> 00:26:35,927
You never know

365
00:26:36,010 --> 00:26:39,097
until it happens.

366
00:26:39,347 --> 00:26:41,224
Isn't that right, my niece?

367
00:26:44,310 --> 00:26:46,562
At least, your niece and nephew are
expecting something to happen.

368
00:26:46,646 --> 00:26:48,898
You bottomless pit
only has a big mouth.

369
00:26:48,981 --> 00:26:50,733
All you do is eat all day.

370
00:26:52,777 --> 00:26:54,695
Let's get Nam-su herbal medicine.

371
00:26:55,363 --> 00:26:57,406
He's studying all day long.

372
00:26:57,490 --> 00:26:59,742
- He needs to restore his energy.
- Yes, Mother.

373
00:27:00,368 --> 00:27:02,912
Excuse me. I'm going to work.

374
00:27:02,995 --> 00:27:04,872
- You're excused.
- Thank you for the food.

375
00:27:06,499 --> 00:27:07,625
Good.

376
00:27:14,966 --> 00:27:16,092
Yeon-su.

377
00:27:16,926 --> 00:27:18,427
Mom, why are you out?

378
00:27:18,511 --> 00:27:20,429
You didn't finish your food.

379
00:27:21,097 --> 00:27:23,850
Because I'm late.
I'm full. It's okay.

380
00:27:24,308 --> 00:27:26,811
Is everything okay with you
these days?

381
00:27:26,894 --> 00:27:27,895
What?

382
00:27:29,272 --> 00:27:32,733
Well, yes. What's there to happen?

383
00:27:32,817 --> 00:27:35,820
After Nam-su finishes his exam,
I'll get you herbal medicine too.

384
00:27:35,903 --> 00:27:38,531
I haven't been able to pay attention
to you.

385
00:27:38,990 --> 00:27:41,659
It's okay. Just focus on Nam-su.

386
00:27:41,742 --> 00:27:43,452
He's been looking drawn lately.

387
00:27:44,328 --> 00:27:47,373
Still, you're my pride.

388
00:27:48,124 --> 00:27:49,208
You know that, right?

389
00:27:57,633 --> 00:28:00,636
- I'm late. See you.
- Yes. Have a good day.

390
00:28:00,887 --> 00:28:01,929
Bye.

391
00:28:12,648 --> 00:28:14,066
Are you trying to
collapse the building?

392
00:28:14,901 --> 00:28:17,862
My heart is already buried deep
in the basement bunker.

393
00:28:18,112 --> 00:28:19,864
I can't get over it.

394
00:28:19,947 --> 00:28:22,742
Stop it. It's not like
she did anything illegal.

395
00:28:22,825 --> 00:28:24,619
You won't understand.

396
00:28:24,702 --> 00:28:26,829
You don't have a child

397
00:28:27,205 --> 00:28:28,414
or a daughter.

398
00:28:28,915 --> 00:28:30,166
Then, what?

399
00:28:30,249 --> 00:28:32,293
You'd rather Ha-neul
just got knocked up or something?

400
00:28:32,376 --> 00:28:36,255
What? No, absolutely not.

401
00:28:36,339 --> 00:28:38,591
See my point? Compared to that

402
00:28:38,674 --> 00:28:40,384
this isn't so bad.

403
00:28:40,468 --> 00:28:43,221
She's smart enough
to handle her own birth control.

404
00:28:43,304 --> 00:28:44,430
I know.

405
00:28:45,556 --> 00:28:46,933
I really do.

406
00:28:49,101 --> 00:28:50,978
But it's just a mom thing.

407
00:28:51,062 --> 00:28:54,482
Even at 30 or 40,
she's still my baby.

408
00:28:55,316 --> 00:28:57,193
Part of me wishes
she'd stay that way forever.

409
00:28:58,152 --> 00:28:59,487
You know what I mean?

410
00:29:06,118 --> 00:29:08,955
I suppose I didn't want to accept

411
00:29:10,748 --> 00:29:12,541
that my child is
finally leaving the nest.

412
00:29:16,420 --> 00:29:17,713
NEW MESSAGE

413
00:29:25,012 --> 00:29:26,722
<i>Fair enough, I admit it.</i>

414
00:29:26,806 --> 00:29:28,307
<i>I was being lame.</i>

415
00:29:28,975 --> 00:29:32,979
<i>Sorry I'm acting petty</i>
<i>while you keep growing.</i>

416
00:29:33,521 --> 00:29:35,523
<i>But here's the deal. Rule one.</i>

417
00:29:35,856 --> 00:29:37,358
<i>Use good condoms.</i>

418
00:29:37,900 --> 00:29:39,277
<i>Rule two.</i>

419
00:29:39,360 --> 00:29:42,405
<i>Always go to regular checkups</i>
<i>with me.</i>

420
00:29:43,072 --> 00:29:44,448
<i>Rule three.</i>

421
00:29:44,532 --> 00:29:46,826
<i>Absolutely no marrying Dong-u.</i>

422
00:29:48,160 --> 00:29:49,370
<i>Deal.</i>

423
00:29:49,453 --> 00:29:52,373
<i>Sorry for making you upset, Mom.</i>

424
00:29:52,623 --> 00:29:54,041
<i>How about a truce</i>
<i>over some </i>tteokbokki<i>?</i>

425
00:29:54,125 --> 00:29:55,209
I'm heading out early today.

426
00:29:55,293 --> 00:29:57,378
- What?
- I'm having <i>tteokbokki </i>with my girl.

427
00:29:59,338 --> 00:30:00,506
You expect me to do all this alone?

428
00:30:00,589 --> 00:30:03,592
I covered all of this when you went
to Ganghwa Island with that girl.

429
00:30:03,676 --> 00:30:04,719
Don't you remember?

430
00:30:07,179 --> 00:30:08,514
For the record

431
00:30:09,515 --> 00:30:12,018
Grandma's Homemade Tteokbokki
over in Hwangdeok-dong is the best.

432
00:30:12,184 --> 00:30:13,269
Right.

433
00:30:14,395 --> 00:30:15,479
See you.

434
00:30:25,823 --> 00:30:26,866
PETER PAN T

435
00:30:26,949 --> 00:30:32,371
THINK I'M JOKING?
I'M COMING TO TEAR YOUR COMPANY APART

436
00:30:50,473 --> 00:30:51,599
Excuse me.

437
00:30:52,058 --> 00:30:55,186
How can I help you?

438
00:30:56,437 --> 00:31:00,107
Sir, I need you to tell me
what you're here for.

439
00:31:09,075 --> 00:31:10,701
It certainly packs a punch.

440
00:31:11,118 --> 00:31:13,120
But the grip is disappointing.

441
00:31:13,579 --> 00:31:15,039
Did she not enjoy our date?

442
00:31:15,122 --> 00:31:16,499
The settings aren't subtle, either.

443
00:31:16,957 --> 00:31:18,918
- This will divide opinions.
- Right.

444
00:31:19,668 --> 00:31:21,253
I should've checked
her preferences first.

445
00:31:21,629 --> 00:31:23,214
Dating requires strategy after all.

446
00:31:23,297 --> 00:31:25,424
Dude, just go home.

447
00:31:27,968 --> 00:31:29,303
I wonder what he's like.

448
00:31:30,096 --> 00:31:31,514
The one Ms. Gong likes.

449
00:31:32,515 --> 00:31:35,476
Naive women like her are
usually magnets for weird jerks.

450
00:31:35,851 --> 00:31:37,186
She needs to be careful.

451
00:31:37,436 --> 00:31:40,356
Come on. She isn't stupid.
She can judge that much character.

452
00:31:40,439 --> 00:31:43,025
Love makes you blind
and clouds your judgment.

453
00:31:43,943 --> 00:31:45,236
I get it. Now focus on work.

454
00:31:49,698 --> 00:31:51,534
INCOMING CALL
GONG YEON-SU

455
00:31:51,617 --> 00:31:54,328
<i>The call cannot be connected.</i>
<i>You'll be directed to voicemail.</i>

456
00:31:54,412 --> 00:31:56,622
<i>Extra fees will be charged</i>
<i>after the tone.</i>

457
00:31:58,290 --> 00:31:59,875
Hello, Mr. Dokgo.

458
00:32:01,043 --> 00:32:04,588
A visitor is here asking for you.
It seems Peter Pan T...

459
00:32:08,175 --> 00:32:10,052
1 UNREAD MESSAGE

460
00:32:11,595 --> 00:32:13,389
<i>Playing the first message.</i>

461
00:32:13,472 --> 00:32:18,102
<i>Hello, Mr. Dokgo. A visitor is here</i>
<i>asking for you. It seems Peter Pan...</i>

462
00:32:18,477 --> 00:32:20,187
<i>Sir? Wait a second.</i>

463
00:32:21,313 --> 00:32:22,648
Dal, where are you going?

464
00:32:24,108 --> 00:32:25,568
CEO DOKGO DAL

465
00:32:29,780 --> 00:32:32,450
He spared no expense
decorating this place with my money.

466
00:32:35,161 --> 00:32:36,662
Before the CEO gets here

467
00:32:36,745 --> 00:32:39,832
let me say a few things.

468
00:32:44,170 --> 00:32:46,922
You're Peter Pan T, right?

469
00:32:47,798 --> 00:32:51,719
It appears you've left 47 complaints.

470
00:32:51,927 --> 00:32:54,221
"The intensity is too weak."

471
00:32:54,305 --> 00:32:57,475
"My wife got electrocuted
during use."

472
00:32:57,808 --> 00:33:00,603
And a bunch of charging errors.

473
00:33:00,686 --> 00:33:01,854
- Look.
- First.

474
00:33:01,937 --> 00:33:04,565
Our products are
medical-grade silicone.

475
00:33:04,648 --> 00:33:06,275
Internal shocks are
physically impossible.

476
00:33:06,358 --> 00:33:07,610
Second.

477
00:33:07,693 --> 00:33:10,029
The manual explicitly states
slow charging only

478
00:33:10,112 --> 00:33:11,363
yet you used a fast charger.

479
00:33:11,447 --> 00:33:12,615
That's user error.

480
00:33:12,698 --> 00:33:13,699
Third.

481
00:33:13,866 --> 00:33:16,744
If these issues persist

482
00:33:16,827 --> 00:33:19,622
I must ask why
you keep buying from us.

483
00:33:19,705 --> 00:33:22,917
You're literally
in our top one percent of spenders.

484
00:33:23,000 --> 00:33:24,627
What are
the annual sales figures here?

485
00:33:24,710 --> 00:33:25,878
And the operating profit?

486
00:33:30,424 --> 00:33:31,842
But sir

487
00:33:31,926 --> 00:33:33,636
your threats have crossed a line.

488
00:33:34,303 --> 00:33:37,223
- Threats?
- If you keep using abusive language

489
00:33:37,306 --> 00:33:40,142
such as threatening
to tear the company apart

490
00:33:40,226 --> 00:33:42,186
or to grab the CEO by the collar
and physically assault him

491
00:33:42,603 --> 00:33:44,230
we won't just sit back.

492
00:33:50,986 --> 00:33:52,196
What is your name, miss?

493
00:33:52,279 --> 00:33:56,534
It's not miss. I'm Gong Yeon-su,
in charge of marketing.

494
00:33:57,493 --> 00:33:58,702
Ms. Gong.

495
00:33:58,786 --> 00:34:00,496
I'm fully capable

496
00:34:00,955 --> 00:34:02,915
of doing whatever I want to that CEO.

497
00:34:03,999 --> 00:34:05,292
You don't have kids, do you?

498
00:34:05,793 --> 00:34:07,878
Has it ever crossed your mind

499
00:34:07,962 --> 00:34:11,549
that the people you mistreat are
someone else's precious children?

500
00:34:12,007 --> 00:34:13,092
Father!

501
00:34:16,178 --> 00:34:17,429
"Father"?

502
00:34:24,311 --> 00:34:25,729
What brings you here?

503
00:34:27,648 --> 00:34:30,234
How dare you make me
drag myself all the way here?

504
00:34:30,985 --> 00:34:32,611
I heard from President Yoon.

505
00:34:32,945 --> 00:34:34,488
Tearing down my reputation

506
00:34:34,989 --> 00:34:36,365
wasn't enough for you?

507
00:34:37,366 --> 00:34:38,742
How much more

508
00:34:38,826 --> 00:34:41,412
must you humiliate your own father
before you're satisfied?

509
00:34:45,666 --> 00:34:47,209
- Step outside.
- I told you to get married

510
00:34:47,626 --> 00:34:50,671
and act like a normal person,
and you told them what?

511
00:34:50,754 --> 00:34:51,755
That you're infertile?

512
00:34:59,471 --> 00:35:00,973
Let me handle this.

513
00:35:09,940 --> 00:35:12,860
His father's a bit rough
with his words

514
00:35:12,943 --> 00:35:14,153
but he's not a bad person.

515
00:35:15,321 --> 00:35:18,073
Don't worry

516
00:35:18,574 --> 00:35:20,951
- and head back to your desk.
- No.

517
00:35:23,120 --> 00:35:24,413
I'll stay.

518
00:35:25,039 --> 00:35:26,915
I feel like I need to be here.

519
00:35:26,999 --> 00:35:29,043
You shouldn't cause a scene
at someone else's business.

520
00:35:29,126 --> 00:35:30,628
This is my company.

521
00:35:30,711 --> 00:35:32,504
This is happening because of me.

522
00:35:32,838 --> 00:35:34,923
Feeling embarrassed
in front of your employee?

523
00:35:36,634 --> 00:35:38,552
Selling this trash for money
doesn't embarrass you?

524
00:35:39,845 --> 00:35:41,096
You pathetic fool.

525
00:35:41,180 --> 00:35:43,515
You call this garbage a business?

526
00:35:43,599 --> 00:35:45,684
When will you stop wasting your life?

527
00:35:45,768 --> 00:35:46,769
I wonder.

528
00:35:47,811 --> 00:35:50,147
Did your life go exactly as planned?

529
00:35:50,230 --> 00:35:51,732
- What?
- You never spared me

530
00:35:51,815 --> 00:35:53,317
a single glance my whole life.

531
00:35:53,400 --> 00:35:55,486
I really don't get why you're
suddenly breathing down my neck.

532
00:35:55,569 --> 00:35:57,404
Get married
and act like a normal person?

533
00:35:57,946 --> 00:35:59,031
Tell me.

534
00:35:59,823 --> 00:36:02,618
Did marrying four times
make you a saint?

535
00:36:02,701 --> 00:36:05,037
- You little punk!
- I'm not getting married!

536
00:36:20,511 --> 00:36:21,679
I don't want anyone

537
00:36:22,179 --> 00:36:24,390
dragging themselves
into my mess of a life.

538
00:36:30,229 --> 00:36:31,730
I refuse to hurt

539
00:36:32,773 --> 00:36:34,233
someone precious to me.

540
00:36:38,529 --> 00:36:40,322
Just like you did to Mother.

541
00:36:40,864 --> 00:36:42,908
With President Yoon aware,
your marriage prospects are ruined.

542
00:36:42,991 --> 00:36:44,243
Clear things up
with them immediately.

543
00:36:44,326 --> 00:36:45,703
That chapter is already closed.

544
00:36:45,953 --> 00:36:48,455
You won't do it?
Then, I'll do it myself.

545
00:36:49,623 --> 00:36:50,791
Father.

546
00:36:54,253 --> 00:36:56,088
I'm sorry to interrupt.

547
00:36:56,338 --> 00:36:59,258
I believe the explanation
should come from me.

548
00:37:00,509 --> 00:37:01,677
Ms. Gong.

549
00:37:10,769 --> 00:37:13,480
Mr. Dokgo didn't do anything wrong.

550
00:37:13,731 --> 00:37:15,649
I asked him for a favor.

551
00:37:16,400 --> 00:37:19,611
To completely crush
my family's expectations.

552
00:37:24,992 --> 00:37:26,827
Allow me to introduce myself again.

553
00:37:27,286 --> 00:37:30,831
I'm Gong Yeon-su, the granddaughter
of Mr. Gong Hyeon-dong

554
00:37:31,373 --> 00:37:33,417
and the blind date

555
00:37:34,209 --> 00:37:35,335
of Mr. Dokgo Dal.

556
00:37:43,886 --> 00:37:45,053
What is going on?

557
00:38:15,584 --> 00:38:17,419
I booked the hospital for next week.

558
00:38:19,880 --> 00:38:21,298
Be ready by then.

559
00:38:22,174 --> 00:38:23,550
Don't worry about the money.

560
00:38:27,054 --> 00:38:28,305
More than anything

561
00:38:29,431 --> 00:38:31,099
my primary concern is you.

562
00:38:32,893 --> 00:38:34,645
Why are your hands so cold?

563
00:38:35,771 --> 00:38:37,105
Why is this scraped?

564
00:38:37,189 --> 00:38:39,233
- Did you get hurt?
- Si-eun.

565
00:38:43,654 --> 00:38:47,241
Is this really
the best choice for us?

566
00:38:48,492 --> 00:38:49,743
What are you saying?

567
00:38:51,245 --> 00:38:52,579
I know.

568
00:38:55,290 --> 00:38:56,959
I know I must respect your decision.

569
00:38:59,628 --> 00:39:01,505
But I keep getting greedy.

570
00:39:06,635 --> 00:39:08,095
I find myself

571
00:39:09,388 --> 00:39:12,432
wanting to start a family with you
and live happily ever after.

572
00:39:16,144 --> 00:39:17,145
Nam-su.

573
00:39:17,229 --> 00:39:19,523
Like you said, I've never had
a backbone my whole life

574
00:39:19,898 --> 00:39:23,360
simply following orders.

575
00:39:23,569 --> 00:39:24,862
But for the first time

576
00:39:26,405 --> 00:39:28,782
I want to live the life I want.

577
00:39:31,243 --> 00:39:33,287
I'm just telling you how I feel.

578
00:39:35,455 --> 00:39:38,333
I'm only saying it out loud.

579
00:39:43,422 --> 00:39:45,674
So what if you've finally found
a life you desire?

580
00:39:46,341 --> 00:39:49,428
What about money?
Raising a kid? My career?

581
00:39:52,556 --> 00:39:53,557
I have no confidence in this.

582
00:39:56,226 --> 00:39:57,352
I refuse...

583
00:40:00,814 --> 00:40:02,649
to live as a trial version
of your life.

584
00:40:22,961 --> 00:40:25,380
I'm sorry about what happened today.

585
00:40:26,048 --> 00:40:27,716
No, I should be sorry.

586
00:40:28,050 --> 00:40:31,178
With your father's piercing gaze
and overwhelming presence

587
00:40:31,637 --> 00:40:33,972
I mistook him
for an enraged Peter Pan T.

588
00:40:37,184 --> 00:40:40,228
Anyway, didn't you put yourself
in an awkward spot for no reason?

589
00:40:40,771 --> 00:40:42,481
I told you I'd handle it.

590
00:40:43,732 --> 00:40:45,359
I caused all this.

591
00:40:45,442 --> 00:40:47,152
I had to do something
to clean up the mess.

592
00:40:49,029 --> 00:40:51,865
But are you okay?

593
00:40:52,699 --> 00:40:55,702
Your father looked
incredibly furious.

594
00:40:57,621 --> 00:40:59,331
Pay it no mind.

595
00:40:59,998 --> 00:41:03,085
He's the type who can't breathe
unless he's controlling everything

596
00:41:03,835 --> 00:41:05,879
and I'm the one thing
he can't control.

597
00:41:07,339 --> 00:41:08,840
Plus, I kind of enjoy it.

598
00:41:14,680 --> 00:41:18,517
Why do you keep
going on these blind dates, though?

599
00:41:18,767 --> 00:41:22,020
I said I wasn't getting married,
not I'd stop going on blind dates.

600
00:41:27,567 --> 00:41:29,569
Does that mean you intend

601
00:41:30,112 --> 00:41:33,031
to continue with these blind dates?

602
00:41:33,115 --> 00:41:35,534
Well, if I'm ever short on cash.

603
00:41:42,082 --> 00:41:44,376
I'd prefer it if you didn't.

604
00:41:47,754 --> 00:41:50,173
- I'm sorry?
- I want you...

605
00:41:52,217 --> 00:41:54,803
to stop going on these blind dates.

606
00:42:01,643 --> 00:42:02,728
I have

607
00:42:03,729 --> 00:42:06,481
feelings for you.

608
00:42:09,776 --> 00:42:11,403
I don't know
if the physical attraction came first

609
00:42:11,486 --> 00:42:12,988
or the feelings did

610
00:42:13,071 --> 00:42:14,614
and I don't care.

611
00:42:15,240 --> 00:42:16,992
There's only one reason.

612
00:42:19,619 --> 00:42:21,371
When I'm with you

613
00:42:21,830 --> 00:42:23,623
I discover a side of myself
I never knew.

614
00:42:25,083 --> 00:42:29,087
You give me the courage
to face things and actually change.

615
00:42:53,987 --> 00:42:55,072
I'm...

616
00:42:57,157 --> 00:43:00,243
not the kind of guy
who can give you what you want.

617
00:43:06,083 --> 00:43:07,918
You said

618
00:43:08,126 --> 00:43:10,587
you've never given your heart
to anyone, right?

619
00:43:15,383 --> 00:43:17,427
The reality is, you're terrified

620
00:43:17,511 --> 00:43:19,054
of hurting someone precious to you.

621
00:43:21,014 --> 00:43:23,141
This path will lead to mutual regret
before we even begin.

622
00:43:24,559 --> 00:43:26,728
How can you be sure
if we haven't even tried?

623
00:43:27,104 --> 00:43:28,605
I know without having to try.

624
00:43:32,067 --> 00:43:33,276
I know

625
00:43:34,986 --> 00:43:36,196
exactly who I am.

626
00:44:28,165 --> 00:44:29,499
So, he won't

627
00:44:30,083 --> 00:44:34,546
give his heart to anyone.

628
00:44:35,547 --> 00:44:36,673
Does that mean

629
00:44:38,091 --> 00:44:39,426
he's only willing

630
00:44:40,135 --> 00:44:43,221
to give his body?

631
00:44:46,558 --> 00:44:48,810
Let's just sleep. I'd better.

632
00:45:17,964 --> 00:45:19,007
What the...

633
00:45:20,008 --> 00:45:22,385
Dang. One, seven

634
00:45:22,677 --> 00:45:23,970
zero, two...

635
00:45:29,893 --> 00:45:31,394
What are you doing here?

636
00:45:31,686 --> 00:45:33,813
Man, it's finally open.

637
00:45:35,857 --> 00:45:37,609
It's finally open!

638
00:45:38,151 --> 00:45:39,194
What the heck?

639
00:45:48,495 --> 00:45:50,872
If you're drunk, go to your place.
Why are you here?

640
00:45:50,956 --> 00:45:53,416
Come on. What's yours is mine,
and what's mine is yours.

641
00:45:53,500 --> 00:45:54,584
Just go to sleep.

642
00:45:56,211 --> 00:45:57,379
Dal.

643
00:46:02,133 --> 00:46:03,176
I figured it out.

644
00:46:04,052 --> 00:46:05,553
The guy Ms. Gong likes.

645
00:46:17,357 --> 00:46:18,984
Lucky you.

646
00:46:23,488 --> 00:46:25,490
Why is it you and not me?

647
00:46:25,824 --> 00:46:27,242
Why you?

648
00:46:27,659 --> 00:46:29,744
I'm way sweeter and cuter.

649
00:46:29,828 --> 00:46:32,038
I'm a far better cook too,
so why you?

650
00:46:34,416 --> 00:46:35,625
I never in my life thought

651
00:46:35,709 --> 00:46:38,461
I'd be stressing over a girl
because of you.

652
00:46:38,670 --> 00:46:40,338
What did I tell you?

653
00:46:40,714 --> 00:46:43,049
Naive women always fall for jerks.

654
00:46:47,262 --> 00:46:50,807
Dal, I love you.

655
00:46:51,308 --> 00:46:53,852
But I also care deeply for Ms. Gong.

656
00:46:57,605 --> 00:46:59,232
So, the choice is yours.

657
00:46:59,941 --> 00:47:01,276
- Choose what?
- If you're serious

658
00:47:01,359 --> 00:47:03,653
about her, do it right.

659
00:47:03,737 --> 00:47:05,363
If not, draw a definitive line

660
00:47:05,780 --> 00:47:07,240
before you break her heart.

661
00:47:13,163 --> 00:47:14,414
I'm asking you straight up.

662
00:47:16,541 --> 00:47:17,625
Do you...

663
00:47:20,545 --> 00:47:21,755
like Gong Yeon-su?

664
00:47:29,971 --> 00:47:33,767
I need an answer so I know
whether to get over her or not.

665
00:47:39,856 --> 00:47:40,982
Get over her.

666
00:47:53,244 --> 00:47:54,454
I'm sorry.

667
00:48:11,763 --> 00:48:12,764
LOAND

668
00:48:12,847 --> 00:48:14,140
Good morning.

669
00:48:15,392 --> 00:48:16,476
Hi.

670
00:48:20,522 --> 00:48:22,190
- Can I drink this?
- Oh, my.

671
00:48:22,273 --> 00:48:23,817
You look terrible. What happened?

672
00:48:25,402 --> 00:48:26,778
I had way too much
to drink last night.

673
00:48:27,612 --> 00:48:28,696
Where's Ms. Gong?

674
00:48:28,988 --> 00:48:31,866
She's running late because she's got
some things to handle.

675
00:48:32,117 --> 00:48:33,326
No way.

676
00:48:35,954 --> 00:48:38,748
It appears Ms. Gong is
going back to SR.

677
00:48:38,832 --> 00:48:40,708
- What?
- What are you talking about?

678
00:48:40,792 --> 00:48:42,043
Think about it.

679
00:48:42,127 --> 00:48:45,004
Her contract is almost up,
and the project is done.

680
00:48:45,088 --> 00:48:46,923
Doesn't that mean
she's tying up loose ends here?

681
00:48:47,006 --> 00:48:48,675
No way.

682
00:48:48,758 --> 00:48:51,386
The pop-up went well, and things are
going great, so why all of a sudden?

683
00:48:51,469 --> 00:48:53,555
Did you hear anything specific?

684
00:48:56,349 --> 00:48:58,726
Just when our branding was
finally getting somewhere...

685
00:48:58,810 --> 00:49:01,271
- Did we do something to upset her?
- Hold on.

686
00:49:02,188 --> 00:49:03,481
How do you even know about this?

687
00:49:03,565 --> 00:49:06,985
I've got my own networking system
for stuff like this.

688
00:49:07,068 --> 00:49:09,154
Are you sure
this is a reliable source?

689
00:49:09,237 --> 00:49:11,865
I'm telling you.
She's at SR right now.

690
00:49:11,948 --> 00:49:13,783
For a sudden emergency meeting
or something.

691
00:49:18,204 --> 00:49:21,332
So, you're choosing to compromise?

692
00:49:21,583 --> 00:49:24,294
There's no need to jump straight
into a heavy relationship.

693
00:49:24,377 --> 00:49:27,172
We can take it slow, flirt a little,
and get close naturally.

694
00:49:27,547 --> 00:49:29,632
We'll grab food, get tea

695
00:49:30,091 --> 00:49:31,885
and talk on the phone
late at night sometimes.

696
00:49:31,968 --> 00:49:33,219
And have sex?

697
00:49:34,053 --> 00:49:35,180
That comes

698
00:49:35,680 --> 00:49:36,848
after making it official.

699
00:49:37,098 --> 00:49:38,266
What if he refuses to date?

700
00:49:39,017 --> 00:49:40,852
- What?
- Let's say he likes you

701
00:49:41,102 --> 00:49:43,021
but he hates the idea of dating.
He just wants to be physical.

702
00:49:43,104 --> 00:49:44,272
What then?

703
00:49:47,358 --> 00:49:48,568
Then...

704
00:49:48,651 --> 00:49:50,695
You think
you can cut him off entirely?

705
00:49:50,778 --> 00:49:51,863
You already slept with him.

706
00:49:53,281 --> 00:49:56,743
The moment your feelings developed,
you were already in too deep.

707
00:49:56,826 --> 00:49:59,370
You know what kind of guy he is
better than anyone.

708
00:49:59,496 --> 00:50:01,623
Don't expect fairytale romance
just to get your heart broken.

709
00:50:01,706 --> 00:50:03,166
Think this through.

710
00:50:03,541 --> 00:50:04,918
Go for it if you're ready

711
00:50:05,001 --> 00:50:06,878
to get messy and tangled up
with him no matter what.

712
00:50:07,045 --> 00:50:09,923
But stop here if you lack the courage
and confidence to even start.

713
00:50:17,847 --> 00:50:19,432
INCOMING CALL

714
00:50:22,393 --> 00:50:23,645
Hello?

715
00:50:23,728 --> 00:50:25,730
<i>Are you family for Gong Nam-su?</i>

716
00:50:25,813 --> 00:50:27,273
Yes, that's me.

717
00:50:27,357 --> 00:50:29,400
<i>This is Seojong Hospital ER.</i>

718
00:50:29,609 --> 00:50:30,693
What?

719
00:50:38,326 --> 00:50:40,912
Hello, I'm here
for the patient, Gong Nam-su.

720
00:50:40,995 --> 00:50:43,289
One moment, please.
Proceed in that direction.

721
00:50:43,373 --> 00:50:44,499
Okay, thank you.

722
00:50:49,212 --> 00:50:50,338
Yeon-su.

723
00:50:51,297 --> 00:50:52,465
Nam-su.

724
00:50:53,007 --> 00:50:54,259
You idiot.

725
00:50:54,342 --> 00:50:57,178
- You absolute, stupid moron!
- Ouch. It hurts.

726
00:50:57,262 --> 00:50:59,055
- It stings.
- You...

727
00:50:59,973 --> 00:51:02,058
We need to tell the family first.

728
00:51:03,434 --> 00:51:05,645
- No, no way.
- Hey!

729
00:51:05,728 --> 00:51:06,813
Why not?

730
00:51:08,022 --> 00:51:11,025
I'm talking to Si-eun first.

731
00:51:16,864 --> 00:51:18,741
How long have you been
doing this job?

732
00:51:18,908 --> 00:51:21,077
- Not that long.
- What about the prep school?

733
00:51:21,369 --> 00:51:22,662
Did you quit?

734
00:51:23,371 --> 00:51:25,498
Are you abandoning the exam?

735
00:51:26,541 --> 00:51:28,293
I still intend to take it.

736
00:51:28,376 --> 00:51:30,253
Goodness, you crazy idiot.

737
00:51:30,336 --> 00:51:32,005
Why didn't you use a condom?

738
00:51:32,088 --> 00:51:33,506
Seriously, this is embarrassing!

739
00:51:34,340 --> 00:51:36,134
You're family for Gong Nam-su, right?

740
00:51:36,217 --> 00:51:37,844
- Yes.
- Could I talk to you for a sec?

741
00:51:37,927 --> 00:51:39,053
Sure.

742
00:51:40,263 --> 00:51:42,348
You, stay right here.

743
00:51:45,685 --> 00:51:46,894
Jeez.

744
00:51:55,361 --> 00:51:56,779
INCOMING CALL
DOKGO DAL

745
00:51:59,407 --> 00:52:01,492
Hello, Dal. It's me, Nam-su.

746
00:52:01,576 --> 00:52:03,161
Why are you picking up
your sister's phone?

747
00:52:03,244 --> 00:52:05,121
I have her phone.

748
00:52:05,204 --> 00:52:07,457
We're at the ER right now.

749
00:52:07,540 --> 00:52:09,375
- The ER?
<i>- Yes.</i>

750
00:52:09,459 --> 00:52:12,128
The accident was
a bit worse than expected.

751
00:52:13,671 --> 00:52:14,881
Where exactly is that?

752
00:52:15,256 --> 00:52:16,758
Which hospital are you at?

753
00:52:18,509 --> 00:52:20,094
Gosh, I can barely hear you.

754
00:52:20,178 --> 00:52:21,763
It's Seojong Hospital.

755
00:52:23,514 --> 00:52:24,891
But don't worry.

756
00:52:25,266 --> 00:52:26,726
My legs are made of steel.

757
00:52:27,810 --> 00:52:29,020
Hello?

758
00:52:29,896 --> 00:52:31,939
Hey. You have insurance, right?

759
00:52:32,398 --> 00:52:34,942
- This is pricier than I thought.
- Yeon-su, Dal called.

760
00:52:35,026 --> 00:52:36,402
- Who?
- Dokgo Dal.

761
00:52:36,569 --> 00:52:39,072
Oh, really? Why did he call?

762
00:52:39,155 --> 00:52:41,199
- Nam-su!
- Si-eun.

763
00:52:41,282 --> 00:52:43,910
Goodness, look at you!
You're all scraped up.

764
00:52:43,993 --> 00:52:45,411
Is your leg okay?

765
00:52:45,912 --> 00:52:47,705
Why did you do it?

766
00:52:47,789 --> 00:52:49,624
You should've just told me.

767
00:52:50,208 --> 00:52:52,210
Have you had anything to eat?

768
00:52:52,293 --> 00:52:54,504
How's your stomach?
Gosh, your hands are freezing.

769
00:52:54,587 --> 00:52:57,382
My stomach hurts.
I'm so upset because of you.

770
00:52:57,924 --> 00:52:59,384
Oh, dear.

771
00:52:59,676 --> 00:53:03,596
It hurts here, here

772
00:53:03,680 --> 00:53:05,890
- and here too.
- Let me see.

773
00:53:05,973 --> 00:53:07,934
You got a scrape here too.

774
00:53:08,059 --> 00:53:10,520
Guys, I'm right here.

775
00:53:11,396 --> 00:53:12,605
Goodness.

776
00:53:12,689 --> 00:53:16,234
You're all scraped up. Why do you
have to make me so worried?

777
00:53:18,486 --> 00:53:21,489
No wonder a child is on the way.
That crazy fool.

778
00:53:22,824 --> 00:53:26,786
Seriously, anyone who doesn't use
a condom should be heavily fined.

779
00:53:33,251 --> 00:53:34,419
INCOMING CALL
GONG YEON-SU

780
00:53:39,882 --> 00:53:41,342
Oh, my goodness.

781
00:53:42,009 --> 00:53:43,344
We must do something fast.

782
00:53:43,553 --> 00:53:46,055
- Ms. Gong.
- Is she okay?

783
00:53:46,681 --> 00:53:49,058
- Oh, goodness.
- What are we to do?

784
00:54:06,784 --> 00:54:07,952
Are you okay?

785
00:54:10,371 --> 00:54:11,956
Anywhere else besides your leg...

786
00:54:12,039 --> 00:54:14,751
Why are you here?

787
00:54:14,834 --> 00:54:16,836
And why am I here?

788
00:54:18,963 --> 00:54:20,298
There was a little accident

789
00:54:20,673 --> 00:54:22,717
by the hospital entrance.

790
00:54:22,800 --> 00:54:25,386
You got tapped by a car.

791
00:54:26,053 --> 00:54:27,764
They said you passed out
from the shock.

792
00:54:27,847 --> 00:54:28,848
What?

793
00:54:30,725 --> 00:54:33,770
Talking to your brother on the phone
made me think you were injured.

794
00:54:34,395 --> 00:54:36,189
I rushed over here in a panic and...

795
00:54:37,148 --> 00:54:38,316
I'm sorry.

796
00:54:38,524 --> 00:54:42,028
Why are you apologizing?

797
00:54:44,280 --> 00:54:46,699
I'm the one who hit you.

798
00:54:52,413 --> 00:54:57,084
Just make sure
the insurance is handled.

799
00:54:57,585 --> 00:54:58,711
Okay.

800
00:54:59,879 --> 00:55:04,175
Anyway, why did you call me earlier?

801
00:55:06,552 --> 00:55:08,513
I'm sure I had something to tell you

802
00:55:09,847 --> 00:55:11,140
but I completely forgot.

803
00:55:14,560 --> 00:55:17,522
I'm the one who got hit, so how come
you're experiencing memory loss?

804
00:55:22,276 --> 00:55:24,195
I'm joking. It's a joke.

805
00:55:37,500 --> 00:55:39,919
I'm not sure I can be a good partner

806
00:55:40,878 --> 00:55:42,004
to anyone.

807
00:55:44,632 --> 00:55:45,925
I'm clumsy at expressing myself.

808
00:55:48,010 --> 00:55:49,428
And I'm numb to emotions.

809
00:55:50,471 --> 00:55:51,597
So, I'll probably...

810
00:55:54,225 --> 00:55:55,852
end up disappointing you a lot.

811
00:55:59,146 --> 00:56:01,607
But if you're okay with that...

812
00:56:02,024 --> 00:56:03,109
All right.

813
00:56:06,404 --> 00:56:07,488
Let's give it a try.

814
00:56:09,365 --> 00:56:10,533
As friends.

815
00:56:13,369 --> 00:56:15,955
Friends?

816
00:56:26,132 --> 00:56:28,718
- FWB.
- Coming through!

817
00:56:28,801 --> 00:56:30,636
- Move aside!
- Clear the path.

818
00:56:30,720 --> 00:56:32,638
- We have an elderly patient.
- We've got a patient.

819
00:56:33,556 --> 00:56:35,641
We have a patient coming through.

820
00:56:40,354 --> 00:56:41,439
Excuse me?

821
00:56:42,273 --> 00:56:44,358
Friends with benefits.

822
00:56:51,407 --> 00:56:55,411
MAKE ME TINGLE

823
00:58:32,925 --> 00:58:34,844
Subtitles by Songmi You
and Eunjin Erica Kim
